# smpnpc.msg - text for the sample NPC (smpnpc.ssl).
# 100-109 look/description, 110-119 floating lines, 200+ conversation.
{100}{}{You see Walt, the pump keeper.}
{101}{}{A wiry man with grease up to his elbows. He keeps glancing at the well.}
{102}{}{A wiry man with grease up to his elbows. For once he looks relaxed.}

{110}{}{Thirty years it ran. Thirty years.}
{111}{}{Bucket by bucket. My poor back.}
{112}{}{If I had the right tools...}
{113}{}{Don't drink it before you boil it.}
{114}{}{Listen to her hum!}

{200}{}{New face. I'm Walt. I keep the pump running, when it runs. Right now it doesn't, so mind where you step and don't waste water.}
{201}{}{What is wrong with the pump?}
{202}{}{A handle that spins free while the rod stays put? Your crosshead pin has sheared. That is a ten-minute job.}
{203}{}{I can fix it. Lend me the key to your storeroom and I will find what I need.}
{204}{}{Let's see what you have to trade.}
{205}{}{Me fix! Me hit pump with rock!}
{206}{}{I'll leave you to it.}

{210}{}{Handle goes round, nothing comes up. I had it apart twice. Whatever broke is down where I can't see it, and the spares are locked in the storeroom chest.}
{211}{}{Sounds bad. Good luck.}

{220}{}{Sheared pin... and I was cursing the valves. You have a head on you, stranger. That is worth knowing.}
{221}{}{The pin, yes. You said. I still need steady hands to do it.}
{222}{}{Glad to help.}

{230}{}{He weighs the key in his hand for a long moment, then drops it into yours.}
{231}{}{The chest is behind the tents, about }
{232}{}{You will have water by sundown.}
{233}{}{You already have my key. Bring it back when you are done.}
{234}{}{ paces from here. Take the tools, leave the rest, and bring my key back.}

{240}{}{Hand my storeroom to someone I met a minute ago? No. Fix it with what you carry or leave it alone.}
{241}{}{Think again. You need that pump more than I do.}
{242}{}{Suit yourself.}

{250}{}{Anything else?}
{251}{}{No. Take care, Walt.}

{260}{}{...Sure. You go find a nice big rock. Far away from my pump.}
{261}{}{Rock!}

{270}{}{Still dry. You here to help or to watch?}
{271}{}{She's pumping! I don't know what you did down there, but the whole village owes you. Here, it's not much.}
{272}{}{Water's sweet today. Thanks to you.}
